  "title": "CHAPTER 2: MOTION",
  "order": 95,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "cm1c3y9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Rest and motion are relative states depending on the chosen frame of reference.",
        "Distance measures total path length (scalar), while displacement is the shortest path between initial and final points (vector).",
        "Acceleration measures the rate of change of velocity with respect to time.",
        "The three standard equations of motion apply specifically to uniformly accelerated straight-line motion."
      ],
      "id": "ak653s7"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Core Subject",
          "value": "Physics",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Key Equations",
          "value": "3 Kinematic Formulas",
          "icon": "award"
        },
        {
          "label": "Primary Quantities",
          "value": "Scalar & Vector",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
          "label": "Exam Focus",
          "value": "Graphs & Conversions",
          "icon": "check"
        }
      ],
      "id": "ojwhg9e"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cuzcuq2",
      "content": "Motion is said to occur when an object changes its position with respect to time and a reference point.If an object does not change its position with time, it is said to be at rest."
    },
    {
      "id": "90zywuy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "REST AND MOTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "n5twdtb",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Rest: When an object does not change its position with time.</li><li>Motion: When an object changes its position with time.</li></ul>",
        "Rest: When an object does not change its position with time.",
        "Motion: When an object changes its position with time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nbuvsm9",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "efmgcnx",
      "src": "/books/Precis/SSC COMPLETE GK/images/image_efmgcnx.png"
    },
    {
      "id": "io5fun5",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "19ekxbp",
      "src": "/books/Precis/SSC COMPLETE GK/images/image_19ekxbp.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8axoc4u",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lw9p8ls",
      "content": "A person sitting in a bus is at rest with respect to the bus but in motion with respect to the road."
    },
    {
      "id": "dh99wx2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "TYPES OF MOTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "pdwvwit",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "ffgl2rm",
      "src": "/books/Precis/SSC COMPLETE GK/images/image_ffgl2rm.png"
    },
    {
      "id": "718w65h",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Rectilinear Motion – Motion in a straight line",
        "Circular Motion – Motion in a circular path",
        "Rotational Motion – Motion about an axis",
        "Oscillatory Motion – To and fro motion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "qdd1h6h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "DISTANCE AND DISPLACEMENT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ph1nx46",
      "content": "Distance:"
    },
    {
      "id": "1m33b68",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Total path covered by an object</li><li>Scalar quantity</li><li>Always positive</li></ul>",
        "Total path covered by an object",
        "Scalar quantity",
        "Always positive"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "foywlge",
      "content": "Displacement:"
    },
    {
      "id": "wspp6z7",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Shortest distance between initial and final position</li><li>Vector quantity</li><li>Can be zero</li></ul>",
        "Shortest distance between initial and final position",
        "Vector quantity",
        "Can be zero"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "kc4psl3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SPEED AND VELOCITY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fscylg1",
      "content": "Speed:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f2vh1l1",
      "content": "Speed = Distance / Time Unit = m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "exh6c0z",
      "content": "Scalar quantity"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v1lc6uo",
      "content": "Velocity:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q3pttnl",
      "content": "Velocity = Displacement / Time Vector quantity"
    },
    {
      "id": "i5bc5ay",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "ACCELERATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cvh1ckw",
      "content": "Acceleration is the rate of change of velocity. Formula:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ufycsfo",
      "content": "Acceleration = (Final velocity – Initial velocity) / Time Unit = m/s²"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w40zvns",
      "content": "Negative acceleration is called retardation."
    },
    {
      "id": "wdad3rq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "EQUATIONS OF MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sm200nz",
      "content": "There are three equations of motion:"
    },
    {
      "id": "u3ys9do",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "v = u + at",
        "s = ut + ½at²",
        "v² = u² + 2as"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "weaxm5j",
      "content": "Where:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iscp6p9",
      "content": "u = initial velocity v = final velocity a = acceleration"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Distance",
        "Displacement"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Total path length covered by a body",
          "Shortest distance from initial to final position"
        ],
        [
          "Scalar quantity (magnitude only)",
          "Vector quantity (magnitude and direction)"
        ],
        [
          "Always positive for a moving body",
          "Can be positive, zero, or negative"
        ],
        [
          "SI Unit: meter (m)",
          "SI Unit: meter (m)"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "zwsi5os"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8ngsyby",
      "content": "t = time"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ehjxjl5",
      "content": "s = distance"
    },
    {
      "id": "3v0t2bo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "UNIFORM AND NON-UNIFORM MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tj6rmmc",
      "content": "Uniform Motion:"
    },
    {
      "id": "y8bkyqq",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Equal distance in equal time</li><li>Constant speed</li></ul>",
        "Equal distance in equal time",
        "Constant speed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iwcaekl",
      "content": "Non-uniform Motion:"
    },
    {
      "id": "c5l7v4e",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Unequal distance in equal time</li><li>Variable speed</li></ul>",
        "Unequal distance in equal time",
        "Variable speed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0t6rtyh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "GRAPHICAL REPRESENTATION OF MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0vpt88h",
      "content": "Distance-Time Graph: "
    },
    {
      "id": "i64s2e9",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Straight line → Uniform motion</li><li>Curve → Non-uniform motion</li></ul>",
        "Straight line → Uniform motion",
        "Curve → Non-uniform motion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "91v3vp0",
      "content": "Velocity-Time Graph:"
    },
    {
      "id": "7rkvnui",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Slope gives acceleration</li><li>Area gives distance</li></ul>",
        "Slope gives acceleration",
        "Area gives distance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "el7e4cg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "UNITS AND CONVERSIONS"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The slope of a Distance-Time graph represents speed, while the slope of a Velocity-Time graph gives acceleration.",
        "The total area under a Velocity-Time graph equals the displacement of the moving object.",
        "Displacement can be positive, negative, or zero, whereas distance covered by a moving object is always positive."
      ],
      "id": "rmjeaao"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xpvux3q",
      "content": "1 km/h = 5/18 m/s 1 m/s = 18/5 km/h"
    },
    {
      "id": "get4lli",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SSC EXAM IMPORTANT QUESTIONS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pir7lvc",
      "content": "Q1. SI unit of acceleration? Ans: m/s²"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wjin2k1",
      "content": "Q2. Formula of velocity? Ans: Distance / Time"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xxkij45",
      "content": "Q3. What is retardation? Ans: Negative acceleration"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l4bihbi",
      "content": "Q4. Unit of speed?"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "12jn0oh",
      "content": "Ans: m/s"
    },
    {
      "id": "i8m57ea",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "QUICK REVISION POINTS"
    },
    {
      "id": "rp9xzyy",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Motion means change in position</li><li>Speed is scalar, velocity is vector</li><li>Acceleration is change in velocity</li><li>v = u + at</li><li>s = ut + ½at²</li><li>v² = u² + 2as</li></ul>",
        "Motion means change in position",
        "Speed is scalar, velocity is vector",
        "Acceleration is change in velocity",
        "v = u + at",
        "s = ut + ½at²",
        "v² = u² + 2as"
      ]
    }
  ],
